A||||5||California Kid||Questions on custom "Curved Dash".||||5||
Z||000000||California Kid||07-18-2001||09:19 PM||||Searching for any information on Custom Curved Dash with Console, see that PISA Cybercars sells it.<P>Would appreciate any feedback. Is it only available from PISA ? How are they to deal with ? How did your installation go, any major headaches? Any problems after installation ? Any info on gage package and switches seen on John Norman's car (ref pictures of his car in Michigan Show post last couple days)? etc., etc.<P>I'm really playing with the idea of doing the swap, have to enter custom or modified classes with car anyway, and the interior in my car doesn't score real high in points in tough professional shows.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jay||07-18-2001||09:42 PM||||If you are going to upholster it in leather or vinyl, get someone that knows what they are doing.  It can be difficult to get it to look good without wrinkles in the material.  I believe John's car is using Auto meter gauges.  I'll dig out my photos of his car from the Toronto show last year.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||07-18-2001||09:45 PM||||On second thought I think that they are VDO.  As far as I know, it is only available through PISA.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/josn's_interior_1.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||California Kid||07-18-2001||10:37 PM||||Thanks for your feedback Jay. I did see a couple cars with the Black Vinyl Dash and they looked real nice. Don't thing I'd take the risk to attempt going cloth or leather, it's already an expensive modification as it is.<P>The bad thing about the Fiero Dash, when it comes to modified or custom shows cars, is that even with some "dress up items" it still looks modular, with questionable styling (you love it or hate it, no middle road). Most hot rods shows I've competed in, their dash'es are custom made, which gets them points for originality.<P>I'm kinda 50/50 on the swap, one pain is that I wouldn't want to loose the two parts signed by Carroll Shelby, would have to cut these parts, and fabricate into new dash somewhere. I don't know if his signature means to much on the car, but he rode in it, I've met him, my Uncle worked with him (Ford assigned him) developing the first Shelby Mustang GT350 & 500, so it means something to me. It also may be the only GM car that he signed parts for !!!<P>If anyone else has an opinion on this, feel free to post. Pictures of current dash under "Pictures of Car" posted by me, probaby back a few pages by now.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||07-19-2001||03:14 AM||||According to John Norman, he modified the PISA dash some.  He said that the fit/finish sucked.  They don't come covered.  The ones in the advertisements aren't what they look like when you buy it.  I'll hold out for Eddy Snaaws interior for a little while yet.  If he doesn't sell the backup molds (assuming there are any) soon, I may try fabricating my own original dash again.  <P>Anyone heard from Eddy lately?<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jay||07-19-2001||06:13 PM||||I would definately keep the signatures in the car somewhere.  I know what you mean, I can't stand the fiero interior.  I'm having my doors redone completely different with the power window switches in the handles and hopefully a more modern looking dash.  I've gotta get it done before September 15th (Toronto Fiero Show).  Why don't you head up for it?  Last year there were about 100 cars, some even from Michigan and New York.  <P>I've found that if you find a good upholstery shop, they can make what you want.  There is a great shop here in Toronto I'm working with on mine.  They only charged me $900 Canadian to re-upholster my seats in tan Ferrari leather and stitched a logo in the head rest.  I've changed all my carpet and head liner to black and my door panels have been wraped in vinyl (that's changing).  I also removed the cigerette holders and had the shifter councel wrapped in the same tan leather.<P>You're right though, no matter how much you do to the engine the interior has gotta look good too!!!<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
